.TH "RECORD\-STOP\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-stop\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-stop\.sh\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-stop\.sh\fR terminates a running RECORD workflow, optionally including any associated Slurm jobs\. It sources \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR and operates in two phases:
.P
\fBPhase 1 \(em Slurm cancellation (optional):\fR
.P
If \fBRECORD_SLURM\fR is set, the script queries the Slurm queue with \fBsqueue\fR and cancels all jobs whose names match the prefix \fBRECORD_SLURM_PREFIX\.*\fR using \fBscancel\fR\.
.P
\fBPhase 2 \(em Process termination:\fR
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBIf \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is running\fR (the PID file exists and \fB/proc/<pid>\fR is present), the script uses \fBpidtree\fR to enumerate the full process subtree rooted at the recorded PID and sends \fBSIGKILL\fR (\fBkill \-9\fR) to every process in the tree\. The PID file is then removed\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBIf \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is not running\fR (the PID file is absent or the process no longer exists), a timestamped message is written to standard error and the script exits with status \-1\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. All configuration is supplied via environment variables\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 if the process tree was successfully killed and the PID file removed\.
.P
Returns \-1 (typically 255) if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
the PID file does not exist; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
the process recorded in the PID file is no longer running\.
.IP "" 0
.P
Returns non\-zero if \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR validation fails at source time (see \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR documentation)\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR
The name of the workflow program to stop\. Set and validated by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR at source time\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Used by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR to construct the PID file path\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_PID_FILE\fR
Path to the PID file, exported by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR as \fB/tmp/record\.$USER\.$RECORD_DBTYPE\.$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.pid\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_SLURM\fR
When set (to any non\-empty value), enables Slurm job cancellation in phase 1\. If unset or empty, the Slurm phase is skipped\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_SLURM_PREFIX\fR
The job name prefix used to identify Slurm jobs belonging to this workflow\. All jobs returned by \fBsqueue\fR whose names match \fBRECORD_SLURM_PREFIX\.*\fR will be cancelled\. Only used when \fBRECORD_SLURM\fR is set\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Stop a running workflow:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
record\-stop\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Stop a workflow and cancel its associated Slurm jobs:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
export RECORD_SLURM=1
export RECORD_SLURM_PREFIX=my_sim
record\-stop\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR
Common library sourced at startup\. Must be present in the working directory or on \fBPATH\fR\.
.TP
\fB/tmp/record\.<USER>\.<RECORD_DBTYPE>\.<RECORD_START_PROGRAM>\.pid\fR
PID file written by the workflow run\. Read to identify the process tree to kill, then removed on success\.
